<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 20 January, from 1265 to 2009.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1265 <span class="tih-ago">761 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simon de Montfort's Parliament meets at Westminster</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ruling in the name of the captive Henry III, Simon de Montfort summoned knights from the shires and, for the first time, burgesses from the towns. It is seen as a forerunner of the House of Commons.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1649 <span class="tih-ago">377 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Trial of Charles I opens in Westminster Hall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A High Court of Justice set up by the Rump Parliament tried the King for treason against his people. Charles refused to recognise its authority and was beheaded ten days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1783 <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain agrees preliminary peace with France and Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Preliminary articles signed at Versailles ended hostilities between Britain and the Bourbon powers. With peace with the United States already agreed, the war that won American independence was over.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-opium-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1841 <span class="tih-ago">185 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Convention of Chuenpi cedes Hong Kong Island to Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the First Opium War, Charles Elliot and the Qing envoy Qishan agreed terms ceding Hong Kong Island. Neither government accepted the deal, but the 1842 Treaty of Nanking confirmed the cession.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1936 <span class="tih-ago">90 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George V dies and Edward VIII becomes king</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King George V died at Sandringham, and his eldest son succeeded as Edward VIII. Edward abdicated before the end of the year to marry Wallis Simpson, the only voluntary abdication in British history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1942 <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nazi officials meet at Wannsee to coordinate the Holocaust</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chaired by Reinhard Heydrich, senior officials met at a villa on the Wannsee in Berlin to organise the 'Final Solution', the deportation and murder of Europe's Jews. The minutes survived the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John F. Kennedy is inaugurated as US President</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At 43, Kennedy became the youngest person elected President. His inaugural address urged Americans to 'ask what you can do for your country'. He was assassinated less than three years later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1981 <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Iran releases 52 American hostages after 444 days</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Minutes after Ronald Reagan was sworn in, Iran freed the Americans held since the seizure of the US embassy in Tehran in 1979. The crisis had overshadowed Jimmy Carter's final year in office.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2009 <span class="tih-ago">17 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Barack Obama inaugurated as the first African American President</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Before a crowd of some 1.8 million on the National Mall, Barack Obama was sworn in as the 44th President of the United States, taking office amid a deep financial crisis.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
